  "body": "## Run\n\nPost-merge gate run 43990986558 on `3f41b8da6b65b8154132878e459d4430e3fb2063` fails `camcraft-motion` `corner_arc_radius`:\n\n```\nthread 'corners_turn_on_tangent_arcs_of_the_given_radius' panicked at crates/motion/tests/corner_arc_radius.rs:194:9:\nWaterline: no corner turned on an arc\n```\n\nThis failure is not the asset lookup defect of #2316. The motion crate reads no post and no machine file.\n\n## Reproduced\n\nThe test fails the same way on Windows, on `origin/main` at `034c37842`:\n\n```\ncargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --test corner_arc_radius -- --test-threads=6\ntest result: FAILED. 6 passed; 1 failed\n```\n\nThe run before (on `fac6c8e8d`) did not fail this test. Batch 17 merged these changes to `crates/motion/src` after it:\n\n- PR #2273 (`d8c710f5f`, adaptive fig8 crossing)\n- PR #2037 (`9f247b741`, rest strategies)\n\nThe cause is not yet found. The arc turns option (#1733) with a radius of 1 mm gives no added tangent arc on the Waterline strategy of the pocket with an island.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The cause is found and named on this issue.\n- `corners_turn_on_tangent_arcs_of_the_given_radius` passes. The test is not loosened.\n- If the Waterline path changed without intent, the fix restores it and a test pins it.\n",
